Reserve OVMF's IGVM parameter area, so no OS writes where the firmware
reads its vCPU count on the next boot.

Upstream's fix, unchanged: tianocore/edk2 commit
a8210e06a2a19814e750e17919f44b18c6fb17c6, "OvmfPkg/PlatformInitLib:
reserve igvm parameter area" (Gerd Hoffmann, 2025-12-05), merged as
e4f99a85545f41ef7ae23cd939484d69a84b6176 on 2025-12-10 from
https://github.com/tianocore/edk2/pull/11866. It was written for the
same symptom, reported as intermittent hangs on reboot
(edk2-devel, 2025-12-05, "commit 5e8db785: intermittent crashes and
hangs on reboot"). acidanthera/audk has not merged it: neither the
pinned 0672a009 nor audk master on 2026-10-13 has it.

What it fixes, as measured here (docs/decisions/0018):

Since edk2 5e8db785 and 38370cf4 (2025-09), OVMF's PEI reads a page of
guest RAM at a fixed address, 0x812000, as IGVM parameters on every
boot: an IGVM loader would have put a memory map there, and a vCPU
count at +0xC0. Plain QEMU puts nothing there, and nothing reserved
the page, so the OS used it as ordinary memory. A cold boot starts
from zeroed RAM and finds nothing. A warm restart does not clear RAM,
so OVMF read 10.9's leftover bytes. The first entry's page count
(offset 8) decides. Nonzero, with a type below 16 and a zero reserved
field: the bytes are taken as a memory map. Zero: there is no map, and
nothing is marked invalid. Anything else marks the area invalid. Unless
it is invalid, the dword at offset 0xC0 is the vCPU count whenever it is
from 1 to 65535 (1992, in the debug log of one hang). MpInitLib then
waits MAX_UINT32 microseconds, about 71 minutes, for APs that do not
exist. A QMP system_reset keeps RAM too, and hung the same way; a new
QEMU process booted.

The reservation is runtime services data, which an OS leaves alone, so
the page stays as a cold boot left it: zero.

Applied by internal/firmware's OVMF build, unless Igvm.c already has
PlatformIgvmParamReserve (an audk that has merged it), against the EDK
II tree its OpenCore build assembles from the pinned audk tarball. Its
hunks keep upstream's CRLF line endings.

diff --git a/OvmfPkg/Include/Library/PlatformInitLib.h b/OvmfPkg/Include/Library/PlatformInitLib.h
index 469c49b6285e..884e381928a0 100644
--- a/OvmfPkg/Include/Library/PlatformInitLib.h
+++ b/OvmfPkg/Include/Library/PlatformInitLib.h
@@ -321,4 +321,10 @@ PlatformIgvmVpCount (
   VOID
   );
 
+VOID
+EFIAPI
+PlatformIgvmParamReserve (
+  VOID
+  );
+
 #endif // PLATFORM_INIT_LIB_H_
diff --git a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c
index 1b0d9a9b851a..dd5a94ef38f6 100644
--- a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c
+++ b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/Igvm.c
@@ -75,6 +75,33 @@ PlatformIgvmMemoryMapFind (
   return Map;
 }
 
+VOID
+EFIAPI
+PlatformIgvmParamReserve (
+  VOID
+  )
+{
+  UINT64  Base;
+  UINT64  Size;
+
+  Base = FixedPcdGet64 (PcdOvmfIgvmParamBase);
+  Size = FixedPcdGet64 (PcdOvmfIgvmParamSize);
+
+  if (Base && Size) {
+    //
+    // Reserve igvm parameter area as runtime data, to make sure the OS isn't
+    // going to use it, otherwise we can get corrupted IGVM parameters after
+    // guest reboot.
+    //
+    DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "%a: 0x%x +0x%x\n", __func__, Base, Size));
+    BuildMemoryAllocationHob (
+      Base,
+      Size,
+      EfiRuntimeServicesData
+      );
+  }
+}
+
 BOOLEAN
 EFIAPI
 PlatformIgvmMemoryMapCheck (
diff --git a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/MemDetect.c b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/MemDetect.c
index 81fa60ade507..937e2b77a553 100644
--- a/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/MemDetect.c
+++ b/OvmfPkg/Library/PlatformInitLib/MemDetect.c
@@ -1240,6 +1240,8 @@ PlatformQemuInitializeRam (
 
   DEBUG ((DEBUG_INFO, "%a called\n", __func__));
 
+  PlatformIgvmParamReserve ();
+
   //
   // Determine total memory size available
   //
